                        kind @decision
                        text "Adopt a fixed-seed RapidHash BuildHasher for Graph::node_by_path, BuildLog::entries, and depfile OrderedPaths while retaining RandomState for unrelated maps. Share one monomorphized RapidHash core across contiguous and segmented bytes, and use native-endian byte-array loads so the contiguous map-key path does not pay the segmented adapter's per-read overhead. A five-sample release probe over 4,000 representative paths reduced median insertion time from 62.061 ms to 48.917 ms and borrowed-lookup time from 118.622 ms to 94.813 ms. Allocation requests remain unchanged on all six recorded workloads, as expected. The exact final tree passes all configured nplan checks and both the 15-sample and final 7-sample six-workload performance gates against pinned Ninja."
