                at 2026-07-30T14:21:18.405020142Z
                author "brendan@bbqsrc.net"
                kind @decision
                text "Port fidelity is no longer a constraint on the Rust source (owner direction, 2026-07-30): Ronin is judged on Ninja behavioural compatibility, not on retaining a symbol per C function. Symbols kept alive only to satisfy a port rule are deleted along with the rules that covered them. Behavioural compatibility rules under docs/spec/ronin/ and the pinned Ninja conformance oracle are unaffected and remain the arbiter. This retires the dead_code allowances on env::merge and env::pathlist and the trivial-function bypass taken on graph::nodepath in c2d6b7e, all three of which existed solely for port fidelity."
